import GaloisForLFunctions.BezoutValuationIncidence.ValuationVisibilityClockAndRamanujanSupport

/-!
# Pillar VIII: `p`-Adic Valuation-Clock Filter Law, Exact Dipole Wavelets, and Prime-Power Phase Recovery (`ClockScheduleSynthesisAndPrimePowerPhaseRecovery`)

In `ValuationClockChainBridge` (Pillar I), we established that the valuation visibility clock
`lagVisibilityClock d = d / rad(d)` reconstructs the von Mangoldt function `Λ(d)` via
`Λ(d) = log(d / lagVisibilityClock d)` on prime powers and determines the first visibility threshold
`L = lagVisibilityClock(p^(a+1)) = p^a`.

To elevate valuation-clock analysis into a complete **harmonic and wavelet calculus on `p`-adic
prime-power chains**, this eighth foundational pillar of **Trans-Horizon Arithmetic–Archimedean
Incidence Mechanics** proves the **Complete `p`-Adic Clock Filter Response Table** and discovers the
**Exact `p`-Adic Clock Dipole Wavelet** generated by consecutive clock lags `p^a` and `p^(a-1)`:

## Core Main Theorems (100% Unconditional)

1. **Complete Three-Zone `p`-Adic Valuation-Clock Filter Law
   (`sieveLagMultiplier_prime_pow_of_le`, `ramanujanLagCoefficient_prime_pow_of_le`,
   `sieveLagMultiplier_prime_pow_succ`, `ramanujanLagCoefficient_prime_pow_succ`,
   `sieveLagMultiplier_prime_pow_of_gt`, `ramanujanLagCoefficient_prime_pow_of_gt`)**:
   For every prime `p`, clock exponent `a : ℕ` (lag `L = p^a = lagVisibilityClock(p^(a+1))`), and
   mode exponent `b : ℕ` (mode `q = p^b`):
   - **Passband (`b ≤ a`):** `sieveLagMultiplier (p^b) (p^a) = 1` and
     `ramanujanLagCoefficient (p^b) (p^a) = φ(p^b)`.
   - **Critical Clock Frontier (`b = a + 1`):** `sieveLagMultiplier (p^(a+1)) (p^a) = -1 / (p - 1)`
     and `ramanujanLagCoefficient (p^(a+1)) (p^a) = -p^a`.
   - **Stopband (`a + 2 ≤ b`):** `sieveLagMultiplier (p^b) (p^a) = 0` and
     `ramanujanLagCoefficient (p^b) (p^a) = 0`.

2. **The `p`-Adic Clock Wavelet Operator & Two-Level Localization
   (`clockWaveletMultiplier`, `clockWaveletMultiplier_prime_pow_of_lt`,
   `clockWaveletMultiplier_prime_pow_self`, `clockWaveletMultiplier_prime_pow_succ`,
   `clockWaveletMultiplier_prime_pow_of_gt`)**:
   Defining the normalized clock wavelet difference
   $$\Delta_{\mathrm{clock}}\rho(p, a, q) :=
     \operatorname{sieveLagMultiplier}(q, p^a) - \operatorname{sieveLagMultiplier}(q, p^{a - 1})$$
   for `a ≥ 1`, every mode `q = p^b` outside `{a, a + 1}` is **completely annihilated**, while on
   `{a, a + 1}`:
   $$\Delta_{\mathrm{clock}}\rho(p, a, p^b) = \begin{cases}
     \dfrac{p}{p - 1} & \text{if } b = a, \\[6pt]
     -\dfrac{1}{p - 1} & \text{if } b = a + 1, \\[6pt]
     0 & \text{if } b < a \text{ or } b \ge a + 2.
   \end{cases}$$

3. **Exact `p`-Adic Ramanujan Dipole Conservation Law
   (`clockWaveletRamanujan`, `clockWaveletRamanujan_prime_pow_of_lt`,
   `clockWaveletRamanujan_prime_pow_self`, `clockWaveletRamanujan_prime_pow_succ`,
   `clockWaveletRamanujan_prime_pow_of_gt`, `clockWaveletRamanujan_prime_pow_dipole_cancel`)**:
   For the unnormalized Ramanujan lag coefficient
   $$\Delta_{\mathrm{clock}}c_q(p, a) :=
     \operatorname{ramanujanLagCoefficient}(q, p^a) -
       \operatorname{ramanujanLagCoefficient}(q, p^{a - 1})$$
   (`a ≥ 1`), the response across the entire `p`-adic chain `{p^b}_{b ≥ 0}` is an **exact opposite-sign
   dipole of amplitude `p^a = lagVisibilityClock(p^(a+1))`** concentrated on `(p^a, p^(a+1))`:
   $$\Delta_{\mathrm{clock}}c_{p^a}(p, a) = +p^a, \qquad
     \Delta_{\mathrm{clock}}c_{p^{a+1}}(p, a) = -p^a, \qquad
     \Delta_{\mathrm{clock}}c_{p^a}(p, a) + \Delta_{\mathrm{clock}}c_{p^{a+1}}(p, a) = 0.$$
-/

open Finset ArithmeticFunction
open GaloisForLFunctions.BiScaleUncertainty GaloisForLFunctions.BezoutValuationIncidence
open RHTower RHTower.Sieve
open scoped BigOperators ArithmeticFunction.Moebius

namespace GaloisForLFunctions.TransHorizonIncidenceMechanics

noncomputable section
set_option autoImplicit false

/-! ## §1. Complete Three-Zone `p`-Adic Valuation-Clock Filter Law -/

/-- **Passband Law (`b ≤ a`) for `sieveLagMultiplier` (`sieveLagMultiplier_prime_pow_of_le`):**
For every prime `p` and exponents `b ≤ a`, the prime power `p^b` divides the clock lag `p^a`, so
`sieveLagMultiplier (p ^ b) (p ^ a) = 1`. -/
theorem sieveLagMultiplier_prime_pow_of_le {p b a : ℕ} (hp : p.Prime) (hba : b ≤ a) :
    sieveLagMultiplier (p ^ b) (p ^ a) = 1 := by
  have hdvd : p ^ b ∣ p ^ a := Nat.pow_dvd_pow p hba
  have hgcd : Nat.gcd (p ^ b) (p ^ a) = p ^ b := Nat.gcd_eq_left hdvd
  have hpos : 0 < p ^ b := pow_pos hp.pos b
  rw [sieveLagMultiplier_eq_moebius_totient_quotient, hgcd, Nat.div_self hpos]
  unfold moebiusReal
  simp

/-- **Passband Law (`b ≤ a`) for `ramanujanLagCoefficient`
(`ramanujanLagCoefficient_prime_pow_of_le`):**
For every prime `p` and exponents `b ≤ a`, `ramanujanLagCoefficient (p ^ b) (p ^ a) = φ(p ^ b)`. -/
theorem ramanujanLagCoefficient_prime_pow_of_le {p b a : ℕ} (hp : p.Prime) (hba : b ≤ a) :
    ramanujanLagCoefficient (p ^ b) (p ^ a) = ((p ^ b).totient : ℝ) := by
  rw [ramanujanLagCoefficient_eq_totient_mul, sieveLagMultiplier_prime_pow_of_le hp hba, mul_one]

/-- **Critical Clock Frontier Law (`b = a + 1`) for `sieveLagMultiplier`
(`sieveLagMultiplier_prime_pow_succ`):**
For every prime `p` and `a : ℕ`, at the visibility clock `p^a = lagVisibilityClock (p^(a+1))`:
`sieveLagMultiplier (p ^ (a + 1)) (p ^ a) = -1 / ((p : ℝ) - 1)`. -/
theorem sieveLagMultiplier_prime_pow_succ (p a : ℕ) (hp : p.Prime) :
    sieveLagMultiplier (p ^ (a + 1)) (p ^ a) = -1 / ((p : ℝ) - 1) := by
  have hdvd : p ^ a ∣ p ^ (a + 1) := Nat.pow_dvd_pow p (Nat.le_succ a)
  have hgcd : Nat.gcd (p ^ (a + 1)) (p ^ a) = p ^ a := Nat.gcd_eq_right hdvd
  have hquot : p ^ (a + 1) / p ^ a = p := by
    rw [pow_succ']
    exact Nat.mul_div_cancel p (pow_pos hp.pos a)
  rw [sieveLagMultiplier_eq_moebius_totient_quotient, hgcd, hquot,
    Nat.totient_prime hp]
  unfold moebiusReal
  rw [ArithmeticFunction.moebius_apply_prime hp]
  have hp1 : 1 ≤ p := hp.one_lt.le
  simp [Nat.cast_sub hp1]

/-- **Critical Clock Frontier Law (`b = a + 1`) for `ramanujanLagCoefficient`
(`ramanujanLagCoefficient_prime_pow_succ`):**
For every prime `p` and `a : ℕ`:
`ramanujanLagCoefficient (p ^ (a + 1)) (p ^ a) = -((p ^ a : ℕ) : ℝ)`. -/
theorem ramanujanLagCoefficient_prime_pow_succ (p a : ℕ) (hp : p.Prime) :
    ramanujanLagCoefficient (p ^ (a + 1)) (p ^ a) = -((p ^ a : ℕ) : ℝ) := by
  rw [ramanujanLagCoefficient_eq_totient_mul, sieveLagMultiplier_prime_pow_succ p a hp,
    Nat.totient_prime_pow hp (Nat.succ_pos a), Nat.succ_sub_one]
  have hp1 : 1 ≤ p := hp.one_lt.le
  have hp_ne : ((p : ℝ) - 1) ≠ 0 := by
    have : (1 : ℝ) < (p : ℝ) := by exact_mod_cast hp.one_lt
    linarith
  push_cast [Nat.cast_sub hp1]
  field_simp [hp_ne]

/-- **Stopband Law (`a + 2 ≤ b`) for `sieveLagMultiplier`
(`sieveLagMultiplier_prime_pow_of_gt`):**
For every prime `p` and exponents `a + 2 ≤ b`, the visibility clock `p^(b-1)` strictly exceeds `p^a`,
so `sieveLagMultiplier (p ^ b) (p ^ a) = 0`. -/
theorem sieveLagMultiplier_prime_pow_of_gt {p b a : ℕ} (hp : p.Prime) (hab : a + 2 ≤ b) :
    sieveLagMultiplier (p ^ b) (p ^ a) = 0 := by
  by_contra hne
  obtain ⟨_, hdvd⟩ := (sieveLagMultiplier_ne_zero_iff (p ^ b) (p ^ a)).mp hne
  have hb_eq : b = (b - 1) + 1 := by omega
  rw [hb_eq, lagVisibilityClock_prime_power p (b - 1) hp] at hdvd
  have hle : p ^ (b - 1) ≤ p ^ a := Nat.le_of_dvd (pow_pos hp.pos a) hdvd
  have hlt : p ^ a < p ^ (b - 1) := (Nat.pow_lt_pow_iff_right hp.one_lt).mpr (by omega)
  omega

/-- **Stopband Law (`a + 2 ≤ b`) for `ramanujanLagCoefficient`
(`ramanujanLagCoefficient_prime_pow_of_gt`):**
For every prime `p` and exponents `a + 2 ≤ b`, `ramanujanLagCoefficient (p ^ b) (p ^ a) = 0`. -/
theorem ramanujanLagCoefficient_prime_pow_of_gt {p b a : ℕ} (hp : p.Prime) (hab : a + 2 ≤ b) :
    ramanujanLagCoefficient (p ^ b) (p ^ a) = 0 := by
  rw [ramanujanLagCoefficient_eq_totient_mul, sieveLagMultiplier_prime_pow_of_gt hp hab, mul_zero]

/-! ## §2. The `p`-Adic Clock Wavelet Operator & Two-Level Localization -/

/-- **Normalized `p`-Adic Clock Wavelet Operator (`clockWaveletMultiplier`):**
The difference between the normalized translation lag multipliers at consecutive `p`-adic clock
scales `p^a` and `p^(a - 1)`. -/
def clockWaveletMultiplier (p a q : ℕ) : ℝ :=
  sieveLagMultiplier q (p ^ a) - sieveLagMultiplier q (p ^ (a - 1))

/-- **Sub-Scale Annihilation of `clockWaveletMultiplier` (`b < a`)
(`clockWaveletMultiplier_prime_pow_of_lt`):**
For every prime `p`, scale `a ≥ 1`, and `b < a`, `clockWaveletMultiplier p a (p ^ b) = 0`. -/
theorem clockWaveletMultiplier_prime_pow_of_lt {p a b : ℕ} (hp : p.Prime) (hba : b < a) :
    clockWaveletMultiplier p a (p ^ b) = 0 := by
  unfold clockWaveletMultiplier
  rw [sieveLagMultiplier_prime_pow_of_le hp (by omega : b ≤ a),
    sieveLagMultiplier_prime_pow_of_le hp (by omega : b ≤ a - 1), sub_self]

/-- **Peak Evaluation of `clockWaveletMultiplier` at `b = a`
(`clockWaveletMultiplier_prime_pow_self`):**
For every prime `p` and scale `a ≥ 1`:
`clockWaveletMultiplier p a (p ^ a) = (p : ℝ) / ((p : ℝ) - 1)`. -/
theorem clockWaveletMultiplier_prime_pow_self {p a : ℕ} (hp : p.Prime) (ha : 1 ≤ a) :
    clockWaveletMultiplier p a (p ^ a) = (p : ℝ) / ((p : ℝ) - 1) := by
  unfold clockWaveletMultiplier
  have h1 : sieveLagMultiplier (p ^ a) (p ^ a) = 1 :=
    sieveLagMultiplier_prime_pow_of_le hp le_rfl
  have h2 : sieveLagMultiplier (p ^ a) (p ^ (a - 1)) = -1 / ((p : ℝ) - 1) := by
    have h := sieveLagMultiplier_prime_pow_succ p (a - 1) hp
    rwa [Nat.sub_add_cancel ha] at h
  rw [h1, h2]
  have hp_ne : ((p : ℝ) - 1) ≠ 0 := by
    have : (1 : ℝ) < (p : ℝ) := by exact_mod_cast hp.one_lt
    linarith
  field_simp [hp_ne]
  ring

/-- **Frontier Evaluation of `clockWaveletMultiplier` at `b = a + 1`
(`clockWaveletMultiplier_prime_pow_succ`):**
For every prime `p` and scale `a ≥ 1`:
`clockWaveletMultiplier p a (p ^ (a + 1)) = -1 / ((p : ℝ) - 1)`. -/
theorem clockWaveletMultiplier_prime_pow_succ {p a : ℕ} (hp : p.Prime) (ha : 1 ≤ a) :
    clockWaveletMultiplier p a (p ^ (a + 1)) = -1 / ((p : ℝ) - 1) := by
  unfold clockWaveletMultiplier
  rw [sieveLagMultiplier_prime_pow_succ p a hp,
    sieveLagMultiplier_prime_pow_of_gt hp (by omega : a - 1 + 2 ≤ a + 1), sub_zero]

/-- **Super-Scale Annihilation of `clockWaveletMultiplier` (`a + 2 ≤ b`)
(`clockWaveletMultiplier_prime_pow_of_gt`):**
For every prime `p`, scale `a : ℕ`, and `b ≥ a + 2`, `clockWaveletMultiplier p a (p ^ b) = 0`. -/
theorem clockWaveletMultiplier_prime_pow_of_gt {p a b : ℕ} (hp : p.Prime) (hab : a + 2 ≤ b) :
    clockWaveletMultiplier p a (p ^ b) = 0 := by
  unfold clockWaveletMultiplier
  rw [sieveLagMultiplier_prime_pow_of_gt hp hab,
    sieveLagMultiplier_prime_pow_of_gt hp (by omega : a - 1 + 2 ≤ b), sub_self]

/-! ## §3. Exact `p`-Adic Ramanujan Dipole Conservation Law -/

/-- **Unnormalized `p`-Adic Ramanujan Clock Wavelet (`clockWaveletRamanujan`):**
The difference between the unnormalized Ramanujan lag coefficients at consecutive `p`-adic clock
scales `p^a` and `p^(a - 1)`. -/
def clockWaveletRamanujan (p a q : ℕ) : ℝ :=
  ramanujanLagCoefficient q (p ^ a) - ramanujanLagCoefficient q (p ^ (a - 1))

/-- **Sub-Scale Annihilation of `clockWaveletRamanujan` (`b < a`)
(`clockWaveletRamanujan_prime_pow_of_lt`):**
For every prime `p` and `b < a`, `clockWaveletRamanujan p a (p ^ b) = 0`. -/
theorem clockWaveletRamanujan_prime_pow_of_lt {p a b : ℕ} (hp : p.Prime) (hba : b < a) :
    clockWaveletRamanujan p a (p ^ b) = 0 := by
  unfold clockWaveletRamanujan
  rw [ramanujanLagCoefficient_prime_pow_of_le hp (by omega : b ≤ a),
    ramanujanLagCoefficient_prime_pow_of_le hp (by omega : b ≤ a - 1), sub_self]

/-- **Positive Pole of the Ramanujan Clock Dipole at `b = a`
(`clockWaveletRamanujan_prime_pow_self`):**
For every prime `p` and scale `a ≥ 1`:
`clockWaveletRamanujan p a (p ^ a) = (p ^ a : ℝ)`. -/
theorem clockWaveletRamanujan_prime_pow_self {p a : ℕ} (hp : p.Prime) (ha : 1 ≤ a) :
    clockWaveletRamanujan p a (p ^ a) = ((p ^ a : ℕ) : ℝ) := by
  unfold clockWaveletRamanujan
  have h1 : ramanujanLagCoefficient (p ^ a) (p ^ a) = ((p ^ a).totient : ℝ) :=
    ramanujanLagCoefficient_prime_pow_of_le hp le_rfl
  have h2 : ramanujanLagCoefficient (p ^ a) (p ^ (a - 1)) = -((p ^ (a - 1) : ℕ) : ℝ) := by
    have h := ramanujanLagCoefficient_prime_pow_succ p (a - 1) hp
    rwa [Nat.sub_add_cancel ha] at h
  rw [h1, h2, Nat.totient_prime_pow hp ha]
  have hp1 : 1 ≤ p := hp.one_lt.le
  have hpow : p ^ a = p ^ (a - 1) * p := by
    conv_lhs => rw [← Nat.sub_add_cancel ha, pow_succ]
  push_cast [Nat.cast_sub hp1, hpow]
  ring

/-- **Negative Pole of the Ramanujan Clock Dipole at `b = a + 1`
(`clockWaveletRamanujan_prime_pow_succ`):**
For every prime `p` and scale `a ≥ 1`:
`clockWaveletRamanujan p a (p ^ (a + 1)) = -(p ^ a : ℝ)`. -/
theorem clockWaveletRamanujan_prime_pow_succ {p a : ℕ} (hp : p.Prime) (ha : 1 ≤ a) :
    clockWaveletRamanujan p a (p ^ (a + 1)) = -((p ^ a : ℕ) : ℝ) := by
  unfold clockWaveletRamanujan
  rw [ramanujanLagCoefficient_prime_pow_succ p a hp,
    ramanujanLagCoefficient_prime_pow_of_gt hp (by omega : a - 1 + 2 ≤ a + 1), sub_zero]

/-- **Super-Scale Annihilation of `clockWaveletRamanujan` (`a + 2 ≤ b`)
(`clockWaveletRamanujan_prime_pow_of_gt`):**
For every prime `p`, scale `a : ℕ`, and `b ≥ a + 2`, `clockWaveletRamanujan p a (p ^ b) = 0`. -/
theorem clockWaveletRamanujan_prime_pow_of_gt {p a b : ℕ} (hp : p.Prime) (hab : a + 2 ≤ b) :
    clockWaveletRamanujan p a (p ^ b) = 0 := by
  unfold clockWaveletRamanujan
  rw [ramanujanLagCoefficient_prime_pow_of_gt hp hab,
    ramanujanLagCoefficient_prime_pow_of_gt hp (by omega : a - 1 + 2 ≤ b), sub_self]

/-- **Exact `p`-Adic Ramanujan Dipole Cancellation Law
(`clockWaveletRamanujan_prime_pow_dipole_cancel`):**
For every prime `p` and scale `a ≥ 1`, the positive pole at `p^a` and the negative pole at `p^(a+1)`
cancel with zero net charge:
`clockWaveletRamanujan p a (p ^ a) + clockWaveletRamanujan p a (p ^ (a + 1)) = 0`. -/
theorem clockWaveletRamanujan_prime_pow_dipole_cancel {p a : ℕ} (hp : p.Prime) (ha : 1 ≤ a) :
    clockWaveletRamanujan p a (p ^ a) + clockWaveletRamanujan p a (p ^ (a + 1)) = 0 := by
  rw [clockWaveletRamanujan_prime_pow_self hp ha, clockWaveletRamanujan_prime_pow_succ hp ha]
  ring

end

end GaloisForLFunctions.TransHorizonIncidenceMechanics
